this is the final installment.

56
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,180
Dancing Big Kamearry.

57
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:11,880
Dancing Big Kameari.

58
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:16,000
You really are sticking to
"Dancing Big" all the way

59
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:16,780
Yes.

60
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,340
The setting is the near future.

61
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:23,080
Japan's capital has moved just a little,
from Tokyo to Kameari,

62
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,700
and Kameari has become a crime-ridden city.

63
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,240
This story follows those who stand up

64
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:31,420
to that violent crime,
the heroics of brave police officers.

65
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:35,240
There's romance, friendship,
tears, laughter, and songs,

66
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,380
plus a grand chorus of Chanchiki Okesa,

67
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:39,840
and so on, indeed.

68
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,720
I don't really get what's going on, but

69
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,960
let's just push through it anyway.

70
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:48,860
Yes.

71
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:51,520
As you know, Director Camera Akira

72
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,380
is a thoroughgoing realist.

73
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:55,140
Fake things like CG

74
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:56,640
are never used at all.

75
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:58,200
That's why we want you to

76
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:01,840
